Interactive Shell

You log in with SSH and get a prompt (like [ec2-user@server]$).
You can type commands one by one (ls, pwd, whoami …).

It’s like sitting at the server’s keyboard.
You land in the shell and then type commands.

ssh ruser@EC2_IP


Remote (Non-interactive) Shell

You run a single command directly over SSH, without getting a prompt.

SSH runs that command, sends the output back, and closes the session.

No chance to type more commands afterward.

ssh ruser@EC2_IP "ls /home"


Interactive shell → you log in and talk to the server step by step.

Remote shell → you send one command, server does it, and closes.








